xt"},{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md"},{"text":" for the precedence table and for why that trade","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was made. Omitting the field means ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"allow\""},{"text":", so every existing client keeps working","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unchanged and no migration is required.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"effect"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PermissionEffect":{"abstract":[{"text":"Whether a grant permits an action or refuses it (B1, deny-override). # Precedence Default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deny -> an [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Allow"},{"text":"] grant permits -> a [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PermissionEffect::Deny"},{"text":"] grant","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses, ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and beats every allow"}]},{"text":", wherever either sits in the resource hierarchy. Deny","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wins; there is no most-specific-wins tie-break. That choice is deliberate and is argued in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"claude_dev\/deny-override-design.md"},{"text":" §2.1. The short version: deny-override buys one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checkable property — ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"adding a deny rule can never widen access, and can never be undone by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adding allows","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — and most-specific-wins buys expressiveness at the cost of making “is X","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"denied?” unanswerable without enumerating every other rule that might out-specify it.","typ